SUMMARY:Rethinking Perfectionism: Kantian and Post-Kantian Perspectives
DESCRIPTION:This is a read-ahead event; for papers and registration\, contact owen.ware@utoronto.ca \nSpeakers \n\nOwen Ware (Toronto): “The Holy Revolution: Religion and Perfection in Romanticism”; Commentary by Marc-Andre Murray (Toronto)\nKarin Nisenbaum (Syracuse): “Schelling’s Autonomy-Preserving View of Kant’s Highest Good”; Commentary by Liam Barer (Toronto)\nAriel Zylberman: “Goodness\, Obligation\, and Perfection in Kant” (UAlbany); Commentary by Noa Buckle (Toronto)\nDouglas Moggach (Ottawa): “Rethinking Perfectionism After Kant”; Commentary by Alex Drusda (Toronto)\n\nPhoto by Worachat Sodsri on Unsplash
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/rethinking-perfectionism-kantian-and-post-kantian-perspectives/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 401\, 170 St. George St.\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/worachat-sodsri-nCz_ZgnbtaE-unsplash-cropped.png
